WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.169
-We don't always have
enough time to cover

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.637
everything in the recent news,

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:07.440
so here with the recap is one
of our writers, Amber Ruffin,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.809
in a segment we call,
"Amber Says What."

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.911
♪♪

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:15.314
-You guys,
things have been crazy.

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:18.450
Okay, first of all,
work was like,

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.953
"Amber, it's time to do another
'Amber Says What,'"

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:24.290
and I was like, "What? It's only
been a week since the last one."

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:27.760
And they were like, "The last
one was like a month ago."

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.929
And I was like, "What? Okay.
I'll come into work."

00:00:30.929 --> 00:00:33.532
And they were like, "No,
we're still working from home."

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:38.238
And I was like, "What? Still?
Why? I can't stay here anymore.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:40.773
I mean it.
There's a strange man in here."

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:42.608
And they were like,
"That's your husband."

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:45.711
And I was like, "What?
I married someone who judges me

00:00:45.711 --> 00:00:48.114
for watching endless hours
of 'House Hunters'?"

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:50.249
[ Sighs ]

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:51.951
I'll try to make it work.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:55.287
Okay, so Ben Affleck was seen
smoking while wearing a mask,

00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:56.722
and I was like, "What...

00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:59.425
are you protecting yourself
from, exactly?"

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:02.161
Do you think the cigarette smoke
cancels out the corona?

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:04.163
Oh, no,
I shouldn't have said that

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:06.231
because if Trump heard me say
that then he's gonna --

00:01:06.231 --> 00:01:08.200
-It gets in the lungs,

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.735
and it does a tremendous number
on the lungs.

00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:11.203
So, it'd be interesting
to check that.

00:01:11.203 --> 00:01:13.239
-No! Dang it!

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.407
Too late.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.609
So, then I heard
the governor of Florida

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:20.346
designated the WWE
an essential business,

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.648
and I was like, "What...

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:26.385
time is it on?" Because I would
kill for a new show right now.

00:01:26.385 --> 00:01:28.454
I swear to goodness.
I have seen everything.

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:30.522
Whatever you have, I will watch.

00:01:30.522 --> 00:01:33.159
So, then,
the actor Stanley Tucci

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.394
showed shared
this cute little video

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:36.262
of him making
quarantine cocktails,

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:39.232
and everyone was like,
"Ooh, Stanley Tucci."

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:42.735
And I was like,
"What? Stanley Tucci? Okay."

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:45.438
But then I watched the video.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.106
-What are you gonna make me?

00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:50.110
-A negroni. Would you like one?
-I would love one.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.410
-Great. Would you mind
if I get my wine?

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:53.512
-No.
-Thanks.

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:54.880
-And I was, like,
in immediately.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.083
All the way in.
I mean, what?

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.651
On top of everything else now,

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:02.021
I have to deal with having these
feelings for Stanley Tucci?

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.423
[ Sighs ] Alright.

00:02:04.423 --> 00:02:06.192
And then --
You will never believe this.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:09.929
Insane Clown Posse canceled this
year's Gathering of the Juggalos

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:14.166
because they, quote, "refuse
to risk even one juggalo life."

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:15.935
And I was like, "What...

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:18.670
a responsible posse of clowns."

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:21.574
Then, I found out that
there's a real-life little boy

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:24.143
in Australia named Corona,
and I was like, "What?"

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:27.547
Then I found out he was getting
bullied because of his name.

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:29.015
And I was like, "What?"

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:32.318
Then Tom Hanks gave him
a typewriter also named Corona

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.887
that he could use
to write him letters

00:02:34.887 --> 00:02:37.523
so that they could be pen pals,
and I was like, "What?"

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:40.193
And then Tom Hanks wrote,
"You got a friend in me,"

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:42.528
and I was like, "Aww, what?"

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:44.564
Then I cried.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:47.132
Not because it was beautiful,
but just because I feel like

00:02:47.132 --> 00:02:50.236
the bullies are going to have
a field day with this.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:53.305
Then, Cuomo has been
giving press conferences,

00:02:53.305 --> 00:02:56.342
and I was like, "What?

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.144
These aren't press conferences,

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:02.949
these are TED talks where you
get to be bitchy like this...

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:05.217
and this.

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:08.921
But also informative like this.

00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:12.958
This really tells you
what a low bar there is

00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:14.393
for press conferences.

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:16.662
I mean, this man just told us
the day of the week,

00:03:16.662 --> 00:03:20.332
and he has
an 87% approval rating.

00:03:20.332 --> 00:03:23.069
Then I heard that Trump said
that people could cure

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:26.172
the coronavirus
by ingesting cleaning products,

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:27.706
and I was like, "What?"

00:03:27.706 --> 00:03:31.644
The only cleaning product
I want inside of me is this guy.

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.346
[ Chuckles ] Just kidding.

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:35.348
It's actually this guy.

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.550
Ooh, Mr. Bubble.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.919
Okay, so, now,
I'm sure, as you know,

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.855
a lot of states have told people
that they have to stay home,

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.357
and most people are like,
"Okay."

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:46.792
But last week, some people
in Wisconsin and Texas

00:03:46.792 --> 00:03:50.429
were outdoors protesting,
and I was like, "What?

00:03:50.429 --> 00:03:53.800
Why are these people
acting like this?

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.902
Oh, I remember."

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:58.638
If you tell Americans
it mostly affects black people,

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:01.641
folks will be outside
in a big pile,

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.909
French-kissing strangers
tomorrow.

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:07.914
I do not like to have called it,
but called it, I did.

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:11.217
So, then, Georgia said that they
were reopening movie theaters,

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:12.852
and I was like, "What...

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.720
is even playing right now?"

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.589
There are no movies out.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:19.725
It's just gonna be that one
commercial that's like

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:21.627
♪ Let's all go to the lobby ♪

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:23.562
♪ Let's all go to the lobby ♪

00:04:23.562 --> 00:04:25.431
♪ Let's all go to the lobby ♪

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:27.400
♪ And watch our grandma die ♪

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.703
So, then, President Trump was
like, "Drink bleach, everybody!"

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:34.006
And I was like, "What?
Yeah, baby, let's get wild!"

00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:35.674
But then I found out

00:04:35.674 --> 00:04:38.778
that there was no fun,
new cocktail called "bleach."

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:41.414
He was suggesting
drinking actual bleach,

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:44.049
saying it may combat
the coronavirus,

00:04:44.049 --> 00:04:45.518
and I was like, "What?

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:48.921
That is the craziest thing
he has ever done."

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:52.024
But then I remembered
all the other times I said that,

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:57.196
and I was like, "What? What?
What? What? What?"

00:04:57.196 --> 00:05:00.766
[ Sighs ]
This has been "Amber Says What."

00:05:00.766 --> 00:05:02.969
♪♪

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:04.337
Give it up to Amber Ruffin.

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:06.539
We'll be right back
with Will Forte.

